@startuml
actor Customer
participant "System" as System
participant "Billing System" as Billing
actor "Restaurant" as Restaurant

== 0. Browse Menus (UC-ORD-01) ==
Customer -> System: Request to view available restaurants
System -> System: Check restaurant statuses (Open, Paused, Closed)
System --> Customer: Display list of open restaurants, menus, prices, and item availability

== 1. Place Order (UC-ORD-02) ==
Customer -> System: Submit order (Restaurant ID, items, payment choice)
System -> System: Validate restaurant is open and items are available
System -> Billing: Trigger payment processing via billing interface
Billing --> System: Confirm payment approval
System -> System: Create order, set status to 'placed', insert into arrival queue
System --> Customer: Output success confirmation and Order ID

== 2. Accept Order (UC-ORD-03) ==
System --> Restaurant: Send new order
Restaurant -> System: Submit 'Accept' decision
System -> System: Verify permissions and transition state from 'placed' to 'accepted'
System --> Restaurant: Update queue display and status change notification
System --> Customer: Notify customer order has been accepted

== 3. Update Order Status: Preparing (UC-ORD-04) ==
Restaurant -> System: Select accepted order to begin preparation
System -> System: Enforce lifecycle guards preventing skipped transitions
System -> System: Update order state to 'preparing' and log in console
System --> Customer: Update tracking view to 'preparing'

== 4. Update Order Status: Ready (UC-ORD-04) ==
Restaurant -> System: Mark order as 'ready' upon completion
System -> System: Update order state sequentially to 'ready' and log in console
System --> Restaurant: Display updated order state
System --> Customer: Notify customer order is ready for pickup
@enduml